+## 2026-09-09 — Finite Matter and progressive deposit appearance
+
+**Author and owner:** Angelis Pseftis.
+**Status:** IN PROGRESS; isolated source candidate, not integrated or runtime-qualified.
+
+Owner intake in task `01a086c9-824b-7810-9197-59fb1b7613bc`: Unreal resources must be finite for player and computer gathering, using the SC2 depletion principle. Follow-up: “things that get mined should shrink in size as they get mined” and “start off with multiple clumped up”. This refines SPEC-RES-003/006 and adds SPEC-RES-006.VISUAL. The existing 1,500-Matter standard and final-cargo-then-idle policy remain binding; SC2 patch-specific deposit quantities and automatic retargeting are not adopted.
+
+Inspection found actual stock subtraction and zero-stock refusal already in ProcessGather. It did not reproduce infinite income. Visible neutral stock was reduced to a binary 1/0 by CreatePlayerView, runtime setup used 1,600, and the resource mesh did not change with stock. Isolated candidate exposes exact currently visible stock, starts new ordinary deposits at 1,500, and scales the existing seven-spire cluster from absolute remaining stock, leaving a flattened unlit, unpickable exhausted remnant. Saved authoritative stock is unchanged by the presentation. Historical snapshots retain their saved quantities.
+
+Evidence and task-only integration patch: `BuildArtifacts/Evidence/resource-depletion-20260909/` in the containing workspace. Main source/build is reserved by the gameplay-feedback task and has not been changed here. Task-only patch passed `git apply --check` against main and isolated `git diff --check`. Seven standalone native cases passed with one clang++ debug build: all three factions and both player slots, exact visible stock, hidden exclusion, conservation, final partial load, zero-stock idle, and snapshot continuation/checksum; a full 1,500-Matter deposit also exhausted. This is manually commanded shared-simulation evidence, not AI-controller or replay-playback evidence. Remaining gates include Unreal build, rendered progressive depletion and input verification, HUD remaining-stock integration, and exact remembered appearance across fog/save/load. RememberedObject currently does not retain a resource quantity; no claim of complete fog-stage recovery is made. No requirement is COMPLETE.
+
+Internal source review identified that scoped network entity packets omit resource stock. The isolated network presentation adapter now uses an explicit unknown sentinel rather than falsely displaying exhausted/unpickable nodes. This prevents the candidate zero-stock interpretation from breaking existing client picking; actual multiplayer progressive depletion requires a coordinated stock field and wire tests and is NOT IMPLEMENTED by this fallback. Unreal compilation and runtime verification of this correction remain pending.
